vectorwake reached a shippable client: mesh vector rendering, prototype-matched HUD, sound, bot fixes, published to artifact 8a789853.                                                                                                                                                         
Multiplayer works end to end (join a zone, wss, generated call signs) and maps became typed tiles loaded from files.                                                                                                                                                                           
Web client work: check build exit codes (a pipe hid a build error for 3 publishes), unlock audio on any gesture, profile the browser not native, vwbuf cut Lua frame cost 3x. You land flying; escape opens a menu tree. Weapons are one table model. Bombs never splash on timeout.           
Zones own their rules: settings ship over the wire and weapons are named in the zone file. The tech tree is levels, add-ons, charges and untyped greens. Bounty is derived from what you hold; points are the victim's bounty, so a fresh spawn is worth nothing.                              
